 # NeRF Training Loop
 
-Also called: Coordinate regression training, Full-batch Neural Field Training Loop, NeRF Training Procedure, Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) Training Loop, Volume Rendering Optimization
+Also called: NeRF Training, Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) Training, Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) Training Loop
 
 ## Overview
-The NeRF training loop optimizes a coordinate-based neural field to reconstruct a scene by minimizing the mean squared error (MSE) between rendered RGB values and ground truth images [S2, S3]. It differs from explicit radiance field methods by learning a continuous volumetric representation via differentiable volume rendering, which allows gradient-based optimization of scene geometry and appearance simultaneously [S3].
+The NeRF training loop optimizes a coordinate-based neural field (MLP or SIREN) to reconstruct a scene by minimizing the mean squared error (MSE) between rendered RGB values and ground truth images [S2, S6]. It iterates over epochs and batches, sampling random pixels, generating ray bundles, performing a forward pass through the network, computing loss, and updating weights via backpropagation [S3, S6].
 
